.TH "libnvmf_exclusion_add_subsysnqn" 9 "libnvmf_exclusion_add_subsysnqn" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_exclusion_add_subsysnqn \- append a subsystem-NQN-only entry.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_exclusion_add_subsysnqn
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "const char *name "  ","
.BI "const char *subsysnqn "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
libnvme global context; must not be NULL
.IP "name" 12
list name
.IP "subsysnqn" 12
subsystem NQN to exclude; must not be NULL or empty
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Builds an exclusion entry matching every controller of a subsystem (the
entry constrains only the NQN) inside libnvme -- the caller needs no
knowledge of the on-disk entry format -- then appends it via
\fBlibnvmf_exclusion_add\fP.  Creates the list if it does not exist.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, -EINVAL if \fIctx\fP or \fIsubsysnqn\fP is NULL/empty,
negative errno otherwise.
